=2 Walkthrough
!Outer Horutoto Ruins-map3.jpg|right|Marguerite Tower, Map 3
* Accept the Mission from any {n:Gate Guard}.
** {n:Mokyokyo} - {z:Windurst Waters} (F-5)
** {n:Janshura-Rashura} - {z:Port Windurst} (B-5)
** {n:Rakoh Buuma} - {z:Windurst Woods} (K-10)
** {n:Zokima-Rokima} - {z:Windurst Walls} (H-7)
* Then make your way to the {p:Manustery} in {z:Windurst Woods}, Speak to {n:Apururu} who is at (H-9).
** You may need to talk to her twice if you have a {@k} {k:Windurst Trust permit} as she will mention talking to her brother, {p:Ajido-Marujido}.
* You will receive the following **Mana Orbs** {p:Key Items}:
** {@k} {k:First dark Mana Orb}
** {@k} {k:Second dark Mana Orb}
** {@k} {k:Third dark Mana Orb}
** {@k} {k:Fourth dark Mana Orb}
** {@k} {k:Fifth dark Mana Orb}
** {@k} {k:Sixth dark Mana Orb}
* You are now instructed to go to the {z:Outer Horutoto Ruins}.
* Head to (J-11) in {z:East Sarutabaruta} and speak to {n:Pore-Ohre} at the entrance to **Marguerite Tower**, they will give you the {@k} {k:Southeastern star charm}.
** Make sure you get this, or you will be unable to energize the orbs later on.
* Enter the tower, then check the six pedestals to place a **Mana Orb**.
** Examine the **Cracked Wall**s along the north and south sides to find hidden rooms, which contain 2 more pedestals for your **Mana Orbs**.
* After all orbs have been set, pass through the **Cracked Wall** on the east side and then examine the **Gate: Magical Gizmo** behind it for a cutscene.
* After the cutscene, __check each pedestal again__ to retrieve the 6 **Glowing Mana Orb** {p:Key Items}:
** {@k} {k:First glowing Mana Orb}
** {@k} {k:Second glowing Mana Orb}
** {@k} {k:Third glowing Mana Orb}
** {@k} {k:Fourth glowing Mana Orb}
** {@k} {k:Fifth glowing Mana Orb}
** {@k} {k:Sixth glowing Mana Orb}
* When you've collected all 6, head back out of the tower. When you zone, you'll receive another cutscene.
** **(Optional)**: You can speak to {n:Quh Berhuja} nearby for some dialogue.
** Alternatively, you can use any means of leaving the zone that will not lead you to {z:East Sarutabaruta}. Doing this will allow you to skip the cutscene and go straight back to {n:Apururu} will which lead to a slightly different cutscene upon finishing the Mission.
* Head back to the {p:Manustery} and speak to {n:Apururu} to complete the Mission.

